WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.000
The incident occurred in a peaceful neighborhood,

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.650
without any warning whatsoever.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.260
See ya.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.000
See you tomorrow.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.800
Give me your blood.

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:38.400
Like seriously, I was like “Seriously stop!”

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.640
He just suddenly came onto me!

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.900
And I was like “Crap! Rapist?!”

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.090
Since, you know,

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:45.910
a bunch of people have been dying recently, right?

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:47.740
So by the time I thought “Ah!”,

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:50.030
he was already biting into me.

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:52.740
Then I guess I lost consciousness.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:56.260
When I woke up, the place was a real wreck.

00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:59.200
May I take a look at your scar?

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:04.450
Luckily, nothing else was wrong with A-san.

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:06.940
However, over the past three months,

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:10.120
seven other victims have been assaulted like A-san,

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:11.600
but none of them survived.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.270
All of the victims were young females,

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:18.010
and they all possessed a mark similar to A-san’s.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:19.880
Because of the recent incidents,

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:21.640
a rumor began to spread

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:24.110
about the culprit of these assaults.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.820
Maybe this is the work of a vampire!

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:33.040
Do vampires really exist in 21st century Japan?

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:35.890
Is the culprit of the Suginami Serial Killer Case

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:38.300
the one that has been portrayed in various media:

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:41.050
the legendary monster known as the “Vampire”?!

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:43.000
The Goddess’ Balance

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.220
measures the truth of it tonight!

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:50.060
Vampires do exist in this world!

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:52.800
Put in the balance!

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.060
The verdict is… FALSE!

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.490
Vampires don’t exist!

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:25.050
Here we are, ladies and gentlemen.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:27.960
Airing live from the studio, where we split mysteries and legends in half!

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.620
This is the show that measures the truth, Astraea’s Balance!

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.250
For today’s theme, with the Suginami Serial Killer Case as our main topic,

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:39.940
we bring up the subject of vampires, and question whether or not they exist.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:41.240
Our first judgement came out to be “False.”

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:45.010
In other words, vampires do not exist.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:50.190
Now, let’s hear our judges’ comments.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:50.890
Of course!

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:53.800
Our first judge is a famous authority on natural history:

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.680
Professor Ebikawa Isao!

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:58.110
They don’t exist?

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.950
Of course not.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:02.880
If they do, I’d love to see them.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:07.510
Our second judge is a stage actress who will be performing in “Around 40 Go Home”:

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:08.640
Ubayama Hiromi-san!

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:09.200
Thank you! Thank you!
Ubayama Hiromi-san!

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.130
Thank you! Thank you!

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:13.090
So, you also say they don’t exist?

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:14.050
Well, of course!

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:15.070
They’re scary.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:18.820
I just can’t deal with ghosts or spirits or anything!

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:20.900
Plus, I’m anemic.

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:26.750
Our third judge is a prominent figure in the modeling world:

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:28.030
Yumi-san!

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:31.770
I love manga and movies about vampires!

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:33.540
So that’s why you believe they exist!

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:37.760
Don’t you think Dracula is kinda sexy?

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.490
Yumi-san, you said that you like manga.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:42.060
So, does that mean—

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.770
Yes, I <i>love</i> “Bloody Waltz”!

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.190
So I’m so excited today.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:50.290
Here we have the creator of “Bloody Waltz” as well as many other published vampire manga:

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.880
Manga Artist Tamaki Nozomu-san!

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:58.360
Vampires don’t exist.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:03:59.780
They’re fictional.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:01.320
That’s why they’re in my manga.

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:08.070
And finally, one more person says “True,” and thus believes they exist.

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:27.380
Here’s to an everlasting kiss.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:34.610
The leading actor from the movie that will be in theaters next month, “Bloody Waltz,”

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:37.650
playing the role of the Vampire Prince Hibuse Ryou:

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.910
Actor Hirai Seiichi-san!

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:48.090
Tamaki-sensei says they aren’t real, but in my role, I act as though they exist.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:51.500
Vampires, the proud avatars of the dark.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:53.990
So cool!

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:55.090
Please suck my blood!

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:00.930
So, we begin Astraea’s Balance with two votes for “True” and three for “False.”

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:04.590
We have shocking evidence and guests for you all to see.

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:06.030
Shocking?

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:06.450
Yes.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:08.380
With our program’s best efforts!

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:10.010
That’s something to look forward to.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:14.240
I’m Tokita Yukinobu, a TVC announcer, and I will be your host for the evening.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:18.260
I’m Sasanuma Akane, and also a TVC announcer.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:24.090
And for our final judgement, the voters will be our guest judges, the studio audience,

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:30.320
our television viewers, and those in front of Shibuya Station… Nella-san!

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:31.910
Hi!

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:35.300
We’ll have those watching the street monitor vote as well

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:39.080
and determine the final judgement with everyone’s votes.

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:42.970
How will Astraea’s Balance judge the existence of vampires?

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:44.700
Put in the balance!

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:50.220
“We strive for a future without loss” — Lorenzo Chemical Industry,

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:53.220
“All-around security” — Wolfpack,

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:57.230
and the movie, “Bloody Waltz,” helped bring us this program.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:03.350
Now then, let’s start by introducing the proposer of today’s topic.

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:10.160
I’m Tanaka Nero.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:11.820
Nice to meet you.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:17.950
Um, so… how much do you all know about vampires?

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.590
Oh, they suck blood!

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:20.850
Of course…

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:22.240
Anything else?

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:24.510
They hate crosses and… um…

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.820
Oh, right! They hate garlic as well!

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:30.080
They have many weaknesses, don’t they?

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:34.050
They can’t traverse over water, they turn to ash in the sun,

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:37.730
they don’t cast shadows, they have no reflection in the mirror…

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.620
There are far too many to list.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:42.330
Their fragility is what makes them attractive.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:46.350
Does all of that apply to vampires in your manga as well, Tamaki-san?

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:49.120
That’d make them too weak, so I ignore most of them.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:51.780
Though they still turn to ash in the sun.

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:59.880
So… actually, recently there have been an increasing number of vampire sightings all over the world.

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:01.100
Oh, my!

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.030
There are more of them?

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:03.910
Give me a break.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:07.540
I’m sorry!

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:10.290
So, well…

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:14.810
It’s rather rare to see cases like Suginami where we have many incidents,

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:17.700
but more and more people are saying they’ve seen them.

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.220
That’s because of the recession, isn’t it?

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:22.830
Oh, that theory about recessions and vampires,

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:26.790
economic boom and Frankenstein, and how they’re the hot topics during those times.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:29.490
But I hear that the economy of Japan is doing fine.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:30.660
Here in Japan, yes.

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:37.150
But globally, people are still feeling the effects from last year’s Dollar crisis.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:41.990
Since the image of Frankenstein’s monster is one of revival, it also represents economic revival.

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:43.350
Oh!

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:47.060
Oh?

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:48.470
Yumi-san?

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:51.100
Ebikawa-sensei, you’re so cool.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:56.050
The mood in Suginami from the case and the accumulating number of deaths—

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:57.930
Why does the economy play a role in this?

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:01.030
When it’s doing poorly, you feel “weak.”

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:07.670
So people bring up vampires with their many weaknesses and superfluous beauty.

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:10.480
I believe that was the reason.

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:11.320
Really…

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:14.550
Furthermore, suicide rates go up during a recession.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:20.030
I believe that has something to do with people seeing more and more “vampires” these days.

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:24.930
They’re kidnappers, or rather, impersonators who have been influenced by fiction.

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:28.710
At least, that’s what I think.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:32.840
I don’t quite agree with blaming manga and anime for everything.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:35.510
I’m just talking about the most general opinion.

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:39.250
If you ask me, given how these beings are portrayed in legend,

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:43.880
there’s no way such crooked, or rather, weak beings could truly exist.

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:54.750
Well, with the debate starting to become quite heated,

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:57.880
let’s now turn to the audience for some opinions as well.

00:08:58.010 --> 00:08:59.680
Sasanuma-san!

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:00.840
Excuse me, young lady?

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:03.090
It’s getting late, isn’t it.

00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:04.430
Are you tired?

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:05.580
I’m sorry.

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:07.310
It’s really hard to keep up with everything.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:10.080
Did you come from overseas?

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:11.900
Yeah, from Romania.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:13.480
From the vampires’ homeland!

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:16.400
Well, do you think vampires exist?

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:16.940
Yeah.

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:18.500
Why’s that?

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:21.180
Say, can I ask you something?

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:23.300
What are real vampires like?

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:27.380
They’re… just like how Ebikawa-sensei and the other judges were saying—

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:28.900
Those are just fairy tales, aren’t they?

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:31.210
I’ve heard of them too.

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:33.830
But are those stories… true?

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:34.680
That’s…

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:37.040
If you don’t know if those stories are true,

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:41.340
isn’t it weird to use them to explain why vampires don’t exist?

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:46.940
I guess when you’re from the vampires’ homeland, you’re on a different level.

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:51.980
Now that the scale has largely tilted to one side, it’s time to bring out more evidence.

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:54.350
The Suginami Serial Killer Case.

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:57.730
This is the most recent case—A-san’s.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.770
When A-san awoke,

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:02.870
the scene was destroyed, as if from a large battle.

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:05.670
As we frantically searched for an eye witness,

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:08.770
we suddenly received a notice.

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:10.860
Is that really the truth?

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:11.680
Yes.

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:16.250
The one who saved that girl is working under us.

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:19.010
Regrettably, we failed to completely exterminate it.

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:21.500
Why did… or rather, how did you…?

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.940
It was an order from Her Royal Highness.

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:27.050
Her Royal Highness was feeling very concerned

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:29.130
about the deeds of the humble breeds.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:30.610
Her Royal Highness?

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:31.400
Yes.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:34.940
Our mistress, the pure-blooded Queen of the Vampires,

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:35.910
Her Royal Highness.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:37.810
It was a sudden call from someone,

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:40.920
who claimed to be a maid of the Queen of the Vampires!

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:43.860
In order to make contact with her,

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:45.860
we proceeded to the place she designated.

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:49.760
Welcome to my mistress’ mansion.

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:01.840
Now we bring you our special guest: Veratos-san!

00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:05.700
The Vampire Queen?

00:11:13.970 --> 00:11:15.780
Wow, look at her breasts!

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:17.730
Yeah… it’s my loss…

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:23.730
Ebikawa-san, you seem to have something to say.

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:26.770
Oh, no. I was just amazed.

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:28.710
The Vampire Queen?

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:30.700
My, my…

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:33.700
You seem more suited to be a heroine who gets assaulted.

00:11:34.100 --> 00:11:36.170
Thank you for your compliment.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:38.020
No, I don’t think that was a compliment.

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:41.050
Well, feel free to doubt all you like.

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:42.870
Seeing is believing after all.

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:45.530
Let’s have them see <i>that</i> first.

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:46.560
Yes.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:50.510
Vera-san brought shocking evidence to the studio today.

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:55.570
The huge scoop that was collected at the scene of A-san’s assault:

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:56.990
A vampire’s arm!

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:04.680
Vera-san.

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:07.420
This was collected at the scene, right?

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:07.890
Correct.

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:10.190
A-san, was it?

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:12.780
This is the arm of the fool who assaulted her.

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:14.890
It looks like it’s frozen…

00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:20.910
To prevent decay and possible crumbling from exposure to the sun, it has been sealed in a bio gel.

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:23.580
Which, by the way, was sponsored by Lorenzo Pharmacies.

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:24.130
Right.

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:27.380
So, the cell tissues should still be alive.

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:29.660
Gross.

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:30.620
This is rubbish.

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:32.700
Have you analyzed its species?

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:34.140
What about DNA profiling?

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:39.490
If you’re telling me this is really the arm of a vampire, I’d like to see some scientific proof!

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:41.380
Ebikawa-san, correct?

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:45.140
You seem to be rejecting the idea of vampires quite adamantly.

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:46.720
Are you really that terrified?

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:48.600
No, I…

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:52.940
There’s no need to fear, since we have no desire for your blood.

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:55.910
We have the right to select our victims.

00:12:56.140 --> 00:13:01.050
Then let’s assume this arm is real. Why is there a need to publicize it?

00:13:01.340 --> 00:13:03.740
If it was real, shouldn’t you be hiding it?

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:04.780
Do you really think so?

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:08.870
What do you mean, young lady?

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:13.030
A little while ago, that lady said that they just missed the vampire, didn’t she?

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:15.920
And that the arm is still alive, right?

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:16.940
So?

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:23.040
Isn’t there a legend here about the man who came back for his arm?

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:26.420
The Demon of Rashoumon Gate, Watanabe no Tsuna.

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:28.900
So then, by letting it know that it’s here,

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:30.930
it might actually come to get it back, right?

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:34.250
The vampire who’s missing this arm, that is.

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:34.920
See?

00:13:37.530 --> 00:13:43.210
Th-Th-The audience is getting excited, but let’s see what people on the street are saying.

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:44.980
Nella-san?

00:13:44.980 --> 00:13:45.440
Yes.

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:47.530
Do you have a moment?

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:49.880
You’re…

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:51.700
What? Do you want something?

00:13:55.670 --> 00:13:56.810
Nella-san?

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:58.200
U-Um…

00:13:58.820 --> 00:14:01.520
Do you believe in vampires?

00:14:03.010 --> 00:14:05.670
What are you talking about? Of course not.

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:16.910
It seems there really aren’t that many who believe in vampires, young lady.

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:19.960
How about it? Shall we move on to the second judgment—

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:20.680
Wait.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:23.030
This arm is, without a doubt, real.

00:14:23.030 --> 00:14:26.270
If you’re skeptical, simply shine sunlight on it.

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:27.870
Then, everything will be—

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:33.040
That’s enough. You know that’s not possible right now, so how long are you going to put up this act?

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:35.630
You’re just an actor hired by the studio, aren’t you?

00:14:35.630 --> 00:14:41.610
Oh, but you’re mistaken. I am only speaking the truth.

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:46.440
So then, you’re saying that you’re the Vampire Queen?

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:52.950
Not even I can take this much bull.

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:57.780
I don’t believe you, and I’ll never approve of this!

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:02.200
He’s right. Vampires?

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:05.900
They’re simply fairy tales. Fiction, and nothing more.

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:08.470
Yet you keep going on about—

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.440
These skepticisms are natural.

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:14.880
We have been hiding in the shadows throughout much of mankind’s history.

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:20.920
At times, we would intentionally spread false information to keep ourselves fictitious.

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:26.710
Yet at other times, we manipulated your wars, your economy, and even your religion.

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:32.150
Then why come out now? And on this worthless show, on top of that.

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:36.840
We don’t know who was the one that offered its blood,

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:41.200
but some worthless being with no common sense is taking the lives of people,

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:42.620
which is a problem.

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:44.540
Do not harm humans without permission.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:47.540
This is the absolute law decreed by the Royal Family.

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:53.610
The fact that it was unable to hide its actions shows just how inferior this being is.

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:57.330
So, vampires have societies too?

00:15:57.330 --> 00:15:58.130
Yes.

00:15:58.480 --> 00:16:03.140
With the Royal Family at the top, there are three successors as well as their blood relatives.

00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:06.620
The further out these relatives branch, the thinner their blood.

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:10.130
Lowly vampires must submit to their superiors.

00:16:10.380 --> 00:16:14.010
This is the law among vampires for the duration of their lives.

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:17.900
But for what it’s worth, this culprit is the lowest of the low.

00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:20.030
Its name is a disgrace to even mention.

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:21.500
No aesthetics. No pride.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:24.020
It’s a stray vampire at best.

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:28.480
Don’t you think so, Mister Vampire Prince?

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:30.210
That’s…

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:35.420
You believe that the owner of this arm is garbage, correct?

00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:39.550
Shut your mouth already, bitch.

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:42.550
Mr. Manga Artist, can I ask you something?

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:47.560
In your manga, which hand does Hibuse Ryou wear his glove on?

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:49.170
He wears it on his left—

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:51.420
I…

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:54.280
I am the true king of the night.

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:59.340
I take orders from no one!

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:07.890
It’s finally back, my precious…

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:17.740
Hirai-san…?

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:24.370
Here’s to an everlasting kiss.

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:31.750
Ah, delicious!

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:36.270
V-Vampires really exist?

00:17:58.230 --> 00:18:00.280
“Queen,” my ass…

00:18:00.450 --> 00:18:01.780
Die!

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:05.910
Nelly, Nero!

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:35.970
What? The camera’s still rolling?

00:18:35.970 --> 00:18:41.030
What the hell are you doing? Keep it rolling! Camera 4, go after it!

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:47.220
After him!

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:50.270
What are you doing? Stop broadcasting immediately!

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:51.230
Hold on, Vera.

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:52.260
Princess?

00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:55.790
Leave it. We shall just skip some of our plans now.

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:56.890
That’s…

00:18:56.890 --> 00:18:57.640
Where’s the culprit?

00:18:57.640 --> 00:18:58.730
The roof!

00:18:58.730 --> 00:18:59.710
Go!

00:19:00.770 --> 00:19:03.400
We are on the roof of the TVC studio.

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:07.150
A-Are we dreaming? In front of my very eyes is a…

00:19:07.150 --> 00:19:08.850
V-Vampire!

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:11.320
I apologize for our subordinate earlier.

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:15.330
Allow us to complete the task we had started, and utterly destroy you tonight.

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:17.010
Wait, Wolf.

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:25.750
Your Royal Highness.

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:29.190
I shall attend to this matter. Understood?

00:19:29.190 --> 00:19:29.580
Yes!

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:32.580
We shall discuss Akira’s appearance at a later time.

00:19:33.240 --> 00:19:34.080
As you wish.

00:19:35.780 --> 00:19:42.230
I had expected something out of this farce, but I never would have thought you’d be this close to it.

00:19:42.670 --> 00:19:45.970
But it was quite entertaining, don’t you think?

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:47.470
You low-life.

00:19:49.110 --> 00:19:50.850
What a repulsive appearance.

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:54.160
One’s true form reveals one’s heart.

00:19:54.160 --> 00:19:58.630
Your form is nothing but an incarnation of your own pride and arrogance. Does that sound about right?

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:00.110
How pitiful.

00:20:00.110 --> 00:20:01.520
Shut up!

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:07.780
Who… are you?

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:16.290
I am Mina Ţepeș, daughter of Ryuu, descendant of Vlad, and the rightful ruler of all vampires.

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:20.810
In my name, I command you: Die.

00:20:21.100 --> 00:20:23.000
I don’t… want to…

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:42.960
Hear me, children of men.

00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:46.950
And reflect upon what you have just seen.

00:20:47.420 --> 00:20:51.240
You’re the… Queen of the Vampires? Really?

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:55.700
You doubt me? Then, shall I suck your blood?

00:20:57.450 --> 00:21:00.940
We are the blood relatives of darkness, the curtain of the night.

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:03.470
We had hidden ourselves under the shadows of your history,

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:06.040
but we shall do so no longer.

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:07.470
Wh-Why…?

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:12.780
Can you see it? Tokyo Land Reclamation #0.

00:21:12.780 --> 00:21:14.740
That distant bund…

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:18.980
is where we shall make our home, where the kingdom of the blood relatives of darkness,

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:22.230
The Vampire Bund, shall be formed!

00:21:26.650 --> 00:21:28.990
Now, let us dance.

00:21:36.930 --> 00:21:39.250
Dance with the Vampire Maids!

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:40.380
Part One!

00:21:43.180 --> 00:21:45.130
There! Target confirmed.

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:46.180
Nero, go right.

00:21:46.180 --> 00:21:46.970
Got it!

00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:48.840
Nella, go in from the left.

00:21:48.840 --> 00:21:49.310
Roger!

00:21:52.380 --> 00:21:55.090
You’re the interviewer from before. What are you—

00:21:55.090 --> 00:21:57.250
I can’t have you here!

00:21:57.250 --> 00:21:58.410
What? Wh-Why?

00:21:58.410 --> 00:21:59.310
Got him!

00:21:59.310 --> 00:22:00.310
Do it, Nelly!

00:22:00.990 --> 00:22:03.340
We’ll beat you until your memories fly away!

00:22:03.340 --> 00:22:04.160
Why fly?!
